  "query_preview": "..(After midnight Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 810 AM EDT THU AUG 6 2026\n\nA lobe rotating around a large upper low over Hudson Bay will\nextend a trough southward over the Ohio Valley at the start of \nthe period. This will reach southward into a col between upper \nhighs over the southwest CONUS and off the southeast coast. This\nweakness in the subtropical ridging will allow for at least \nscattered showers/thunderstorms for our area as we move into the\nweekend. The troughing retreats northward by Sunday and rising\ngeopotential heights should result in less convection through\nMonday. A series of shortwave troughs then nudge the prevailing\nwesterlies aloft southward again by mid week and give us slightly\nincreased west northwest flow aloft. This regime gives an \nincreased potential for showers/thunderstorms with a risk of MCS \noccurrence Tuesday-Wednesday.",
